1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,240
A kirana shop sells ₹1,200 of groceries to a stranger.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,700
The stranger was spending stolen money. So the bank freezes the shop's whole account.

3
00:00:09,967 --> 00:00:18,886
Apr 2021 to Nov 2025: India held ₹7,647 Cr for cyber-fraud victims.

4
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:24,221
It restored ₹167 Cr. 2.18%.

5
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,772
Money goes back only when someone proves whose money sits in which account.

6
00:00:28,772 --> 00:00:30,879
Freezing everything skips that proof.

7
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:36,061
Wapsi traces the money, holds only the tainted amount,

8
00:00:36,061 --> 00:00:43,414
drafts the STR and restoration packet, and verifies every number before a human approves.

9
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:47,886
The honest shop keeps trading. All data here is synthetic.

10
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:54,059
The Inbox: hold notices, ranked by the money still recoverable.

11
00:00:54,333 --> 00:01:00,593
One complaint: ₹4,80,000 stolen, moved through four layers of accounts.

12
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:07,071
Wapsi traces every hop and splits mixed money per victim, as the SOP prescribes.

13
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:15,008
The landlord paid rent: likely innocent. ₹4,800 held, not his whole account.

14
00:01:15,267 --> 00:01:26,376
The kirana shop delivered its goods: no hold. The aggregator pool: ₹19,200 held out of ₹5,00,20,000.

15
00:01:26,633 --> 00:01:37,368
₹1,42,848 held in 5 accounts, instead of ₹5,03,50,000 frozen in 6.

16
00:01:37,633 --> 00:01:44,738
Gemma 4 writes only the sentences; every amount, account and date is filled from the ledger.

17
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,839
A verifier recomputes every number and checks every citation. Every draft here passes.

18
00:01:51,567 --> 00:01:56,156
Complaints also arrive as voice notes. This one is in Hinglish.

19
00:01:56,433 --> 00:02:00,273
Wapsi extracts the fields and checks every claim against the ledger.

20
00:02:00,533 --> 00:02:06,343
The note hides an order to release the hold. It is quoted to the officer, and the hold stays.

21
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:09,435
On screen: the sample's script.

22
00:02:09,435 --> 00:02:16,569
On the MI300X, Whisper large-v3-turbo transcribed this 26.75 s note in 0.80 s.

23
00:02:16,833 --> 00:02:22,589
The agent runs on Google's ADK, with Gemma 4 calling Wapsi's tools natively.

24
00:02:22,589 --> 00:02:25,543
Every call is recorded with its checks.

25
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:32,479
An analyst's approval is refused: only a supervisor can approve. An injected instruction is flagged.

26
00:02:32,733 --> 00:02:36,878
Every step is sealed in a hash-chained, tamper-evident audit log.

27
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:42,801
Measured 14 Oct 2026 on AMD Instinct MI300X (AMD AI Notebook).

28
00:02:42,801 --> 00:02:45,989
The golden set ran on a second MI300X.

29
00:02:46,267 --> 00:02:53,241
Output throughput: 55 tok/s at concurrency 1, up to 699 tok/s at concurrency 64.

30
00:02:53,500 --> 00:03:00,634
Real drafting prompts: 773 tok/s (concurrency 32), median first token 0.12 s.

31
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:10,124
1,590 cases an hour · $1.25 per 1,000 cases at the $1.99/GPU-hour list price.

32
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:17,849
39 golden cases: every hold exact, every draft verified, 0 injection leaks.

33
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:26,084
Test world: whole-account freezes lock ₹35.26 Cr. Wapsi holds ₹29.19 L.

34
00:03:26,367 --> 00:03:34,401
Asked for the plan in free text, raw Gemma 4 gets an amount wrong in 48.7% of cases.

35
00:03:34,667 --> 00:03:44,641
Like for like: raw STRs with a wrong amount 4/20. Wapsi-bound: 0/17, and 0 of all 155 drafts.

36
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:50,932
GNN on ROCm: AUC 1.0 on a saturated world.

37
00:03:50,932 --> 00:04:04,719
Harder world: 92% dispositions, level with the rule-based scorer; innocent holders 87.5% vs 69%.

38
00:04:05,433 --> 00:04:10,518
Gemma 4, Google's open model, writes every sentence, and never a number.

39
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:14,988
Google ADK runs the agent: native tool calls, a guard plugin,

40
00:04:14,988 --> 00:04:18,764
a trace plugin sealing every call into the audit chain.

41
00:04:19,033 --> 00:04:24,628
Open weights: a bank can serve it on its own AMD GPU, and customer data never leaves.

42
00:04:25,333 --> 00:04:29,123
Wapsi. Hold the fraud, not the shop.

43
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:34,460
github.com/GODOSTROYER/wapsi
